  "questionLabels": [],
  "question": {
    "text": "In the reaction of potassium dichromate, potassium chloride and sulfuric acid (conc.), the oxidation state of the chromium in the product is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mo>+</mo></mfenced></math> _______.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "6",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The oxidation state or oxidation number is defined as the loss or gain of electrons from an atom, molecule, or compound.</p><p>The reaction of potassium dichromate, potassium chloride and sulphuric acid (conc.)is as follows,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>Cr</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>KCl</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo> </mo><mo>(</mo><mi>conc</mi><mo>.</mo><mo>)</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>→</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>CrO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><msub><mi>KHSO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math></p><p>This reaction takes place in chromyl chloride test.</p><p>The Chromyl chloride is a neutral molecule as it does not have any charge on it.</p><p>Here, oxidation state of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Cr</mi></math>  in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CrO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></math>.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
